les.</span></div><nav><a href="daily-command-brief.html">Daily Brief</a><a href="control-structure.html">Power Map</a><a href="entities.html">Entities</a><a href="investigations.html">Investigations</a><a href="evidence-vault.html">Evidence</a><a href="search.html">Search</a></nav></section><!-- reader-governor:end --><main><section class="hero wrap"><div class="money-kicker">Methodology</div><h1>HOW THE WEALTH MAP WORKS.</h1><p class="lead">A dated estimate, a transparent source trail and a permanent distinction between wealth, income, ownership and inference.</p></section><section class="section wrap money-grid"><article class="money-card"><h2>Ranking baseline</h2><p>The first release uses the Forbes 2026 annual list, based on stock prices and exchange rates from 1 March 2026. Later estimates must never overwrite the historical baseline.</p></article><article class="money-card"><h2>Public shares</h2><p>Public holdings should be valued using a dated share price and a sourced ownership quantity. Options, pledged shares and debt require separate treatment.</p></article><article class="money-card"><h2>Private companies</h2><p>Private-company estimates require a transparent valuation method, comparable transactions or reliable reporting. Ranges are preferred to false precision.</p></article><article class="money-card"><h2>Income</h2><p>Salary, dividends, share sales and business distributions must be separated from unrealised changes in estimated net worth.</p></article><article class="money-card"><h2>Families and trusts</h2><p>Family wealth is attributed only according to the source methodology and public records. A trust or foundation connection is not treated as personal liquid ownership without evidence.</p></article><article class="money-card"><h2>Corrections</h2><p>Every correction should preserve the previous figure, new figure, source date, evidence level and reason for change.</p></article></section><section class="section wrap money-warning"><strong>Boundary: